From 266f337b5f475ef434a5c386d900c92445ea9c80 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moWerk <mo@mowerk.net>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 03:04:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: boe-bf060y8m-aj0: send the brightness before
 display on
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The on sequence never set the brightness. Out of sleep the panel ran at
its power-on level until drm_panel_enable() enabled the backlight after
the sequence, which wrote the stored, dimmed level, and the compositor
then faded up: every wake flashed bright, dimmed and ramped up again.
Send the backlight's level, 0 while it is still disabled, before
display on.

Disclosure: LLMGD-0 · origin O1 (author reported the bright-dim-ramp wake, the model traced it to the on sequence and wrote the change; not yet run on the device)
LLMGD: v0.3; assurance=A0; flags=none; origin=O1; origin_headline=O1; scope=kernel; graded-by=model; retrieval=none
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-boe-bf060y8m-aj0.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-boe-bf060y8m-aj0.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-boe-bf060y8m-aj0.c
index 28e88c0c0..137e7e1d8 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-boe-bf060y8m-aj0.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-boe-bf060y8m-aj0.c
@@ -81,6 +81,16 @@ static int boe_bf060y8m_aj0_on(struct boe_bf060y8m_aj0 *boe)
 
 	mipi_dsi_msleep(&dsi_ctx, 30);
 
+	/*
+	 * Out of sleep the panel runs at its power-on brightness until the
+	 * backlight is enabled after this sequence: send the backlight's
+	 * level (0 while it is still disabled) before the display goes on, so
+	 * a wake does not flash bright, dim, then ramp up.
+	 */
+	if (boe->panel.backlight)
+		mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_brightness_multi(&dsi_ctx,
+				backlight_get_brightness(boe->panel.backlight));
+
 	mipi_dsi_dcs_set_display_on_multi(&dsi_ctx);
 	mipi_dsi_msleep(&dsi_ctx, 50);
 
-- 
